  OTLP protocol (all five packages). OTLP log export requests
  (ExportLogsServiceRequest) and responses follow the OpenTelemetry protocol
  specification and opentelemetry-proto (Copyright The OpenTelemetry Authors,
  Apache-2.0, https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-proto). TypeScript
  serializes them with @opentelemetry/otlp-transformer, Rust with the
  opentelemetry-proto crate (prost/tonic), Go with go.opentelemetry.io/proto/otlp,
  Python with the opentelemetry-proto package; the Java package contains a
  minimal protobuf encoder/decoder written for this SDK that uses the message
  and field numbers of opentelemetry-proto logs v1 (no code copied). The gRPC
  method name opentelemetry.proto.collector.logs.v1.LogsService/Export is taken
  from the same protos.

  Spans are exported with the official OpenTelemetry SDKs and OTLP exporters
  of each language (Apache-2.0): @opentelemetry/exporter-trace-otlp-proto and
  -otlp-grpc with @grpc/grpc-js for TypeScript; opentelemetry-otlp for Rust;
  go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace for Go;
  opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http (and the optional -proto-grpc) for
  Python; io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-exporter-otlp for Java (gRPC log
  export over OkHttp, Apache-2.0).

  SigNoz query API. Request bodies and response field names of the SigNoz
  query service (/api/v5/query_range, /api/v4/traces/{id}/waterfall,
  /api/v3/logs/livetail, /api/v1/fields/*, /api/v1/dependency_graph, health and
  version) and the SIGNOZ-API-KEY / signoz-ingestion-key header names were
  taken from the public SigNoz documentation and from responses of the
  signoz/signoz-community:v0.150.0 container (SigNoz core, MIT licence,
  Copyright SigNoz, Inc.). No SigNoz code is copied and no enterprise (ee/)
  endpoint is used. Note: the community image reports an empty server version,
  so serverVersion() raises UNSUPPORTED against it.

  Notable other runtime dependencies of the service code: undici (MIT) for
  TypeScript; reqwest, tonic, prost and base64 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) for Rust;
  google.golang.org/grpc (Apache-2.0) for Go; httpx (BSD-3-Clause), protobuf
  (BSD-3-Clause) and the optional grpcio (Apache-2.0) for Python;
  jackson-databind and okhttp (Apache-2.0) for Java.
